Claude suggested the two following approaches.
{code:java}
Two ways to sequence it:

Full unification (best): move the topic DescribeConfigs path onto KafkaConfigSchema.resolveEffectiveTopicConfigs, decorating the ConfigEntrys for the response. Scope to topics, gate behind thorough parity tests (source, values, included keys, synonyms).

Cheap first step (low risk): extract just the inclusion rule — "non-internal always; internal/unknown only if explicitly set" — into one shared helper both sides call, so they can't silently drift even before the value-resolution is unified. {code}

