{noformat}
poll#1 count=5 position=5  endOffset=16   (offsets 0..4)
poll#2 count=0 position=10 endOffset=16   (skips removed offsets 5..9: empty, but not at the end)
poll#3 count=5 position=15 endOffset=16   (offsets 10..14)
{noformat}

The consumer behavior is expected (KAFKA-14865 tracks it). This ticket only fixes the tester.

Fix: get the end offsets before consuming, and poll until the position of every partition reaches its end offset, with an overall timeout.

